      "description": "Each container against its own mem_limit, not against the Pi's total RAM. Reaching 100% means the kernel kills it, so anything sitting above the 80% line needs a bigger cap or a look at what it is holding. Containers without mem_limit report a limit of 0 and are filtered out: their real ceiling is host RAM, on the RAM used gauge above.",
